{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QIntegerMassFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QIntegerMassFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.fits_AME_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.fits_AME_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L169-L179","doc":"**Downstream conditional theorem (AGENTS.md §3b-cond).**\nConditional on `[QIntegerMassFormula]`, every (Z, N) admits a\nrelative residual `δ` with `|δ| ≤ tolerance` between the AME\nbinding energy and the seven-term prediction. Fully verified\nby Lean once an instance is fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.fits_AME","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.fits_AME","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L164-L164","doc":"**Conjectural accuracy.** For every (Z, N) with a measured\nbinding energy `B_AME` in the AME database, the seven-term\nformula matches to within `tolerance` of the experimental value.\nThis is the conjecture proper; the `sorry` in a concrete\ninstance carries this assertion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance_bound","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L158-L158","doc":"Tolerance is positive and bounded by 1% (manuscript bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.tolerance","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L156-L156","doc":"Tolerance of the seven-term q-integer fit to AME binding\nenergies (conjectured ~1% per manuscript scorecard). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.f_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.f_magic","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L153-L153","doc":"Magic-proximity function. Peaks at the nuclear magic numbers\n{2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}; smooth decay between magics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula.mk","kind":"ctor","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QIntegerMassFormula","kind":"class","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L133-L167","doc":"**Conjecture class.** An instance asserts the existence of:\n(i) the magic-proximity function `f_magic : ℕ → ℝ` peaking at\n    {2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126},\n(ii) a CODATA-accuracy bound: for every (Z, N) with binding\n     energy in the AME database, the q-integer formula matches\n     to within `tolerance`.\n\nThe `tolerance` value is the conjectured precision (currently\n~1% per the manuscript Ch 11 §8 scorecard); a rigorous\nderivation would pin it from categorical first principles.\n\n`sorry` in any concrete instance is understood as **conjecture**,\nnot missing proof. Downstream blocks may take\n`[QIntegerMassFormula]` as an explicit hypothesis to remain\n`theorem`/`proposition` per AGENTS.md §3b-cond.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] Ch 11 §8, conj:q-integer-mass-formula ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-integer-mass-formula","label":"conj:q-integer-mass-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.binding_energy_bw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.binding_energy_bw","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L92-L113","doc":"Seven-term binding energy with q-integer coefficients.\nIncludes the five standard terms plus exchange Coulomb (term 6)\nand magic shell correction (term 7).\n\nThe shell correction uses a magic proximity function f(x) that\npeaks at magic numbers {2,8,20,28,50,82,126}.  This function is\nleft abstract here; the computational implementation uses a\nGaussian with σ = 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.exchange_coulomb_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.exchange_coulomb_relation","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L80-L88","doc":"The exchange-to-Coulomb ratio is the nucleon screening factor:\nλ_ex · (q-q⁻¹) · [6]_q · [2]_q = λ_C · [3]_q.\nBoth sides equal (q-q⁻¹) · [3]_q · [6]_q · m_e when expanded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.asym_volume_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.asym_volume_relation","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L73-L78","doc":"The relation a_asym = (3/2) × λ_V holds exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.delta_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.delta_S","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L62-L69","doc":"Shell correction coefficient δ_S = [2]_q² · [3]_q · m_e.\nProduct of pair-interaction dimension squared ([2]_q²) and\nnucleon strand count ([3]_q).  Active at magic-number closures\nwhere torus knot T_{2,m} coherence aligns exceptional divisors.\nSee conj:shell-closure-nf-term-count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_ex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_ex","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L55-L60","doc":"Exchange Coulomb coefficient λ_ex = [3]_q/[2]_q · m_e.\nThe ratio [3]_q/[2]_q is the nucleon screening factor:\nthe 3-strand internal structure partially screens pp repulsion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.delta_P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.delta_P","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L49-L51","doc":"Pairing coefficient δ_P = [3]_q[7]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.a_asym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.a_asym","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L45-L47","doc":"Asymmetry coefficient a_asym = 3[2]_q[7]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_C","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L41-L43","doc":"Coulomb coefficient λ_C = (q - q⁻¹)[6]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_S","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Surface coefficient λ_S = 2[4]_q² · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.lambda_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.lambda_V","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L32-L35","doc":"Volume coefficient λ_V = 2[2]_q[7]_q · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.q_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.q_int","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-integer-mass-formula.lean#L26-L28","doc":"Quantum integer [n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n}) / (q - q^{-1}). ","signatureChunk":0}]}